# Micro App source constraints

These files are transpiled in the browser and injected into a host page that
already loads every library. They are **not** bundled.

- No `import` / `require` — libraries are globals. Read the current list from the
  `fulfil://guide/micro-apps` resource on the fulfil MCP server before writing code.
- No HTML shell, no `<script>` tags — the page is generated.
- No auth code, API keys, `.env`, or CORS handling — the app runs same-origin on
  the user's Fulfil session.
- No build config for the app itself.
- `app.jsx` is the entry point and must render into `#root`.

## Data

All data access goes through `window.__FULFIL__`. Wrap every call: when one
fails, render the error in the UI. A chart that silently renders empty because
the call was refused is a bug, not a fallback.
